{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA + fix (rebar-debug protocol, Option A)\n\n**Problem.** Autodeploy deploys containers and swaps the `/mcp/` upstream include, but the nginx edge source of truth `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` is absent from every path manifest in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`, so a merged edge change is never detected and — unlike a Gerrit config change (`AUTODEPLOY_ERROR reason=config_manual`) — emits NO signal. It fails silently.\n\n**Proven root cause (mechanism).** `changed() { changed_range \"$DEPLOYED\" \"$TARGET\" \"$1\"; }` is only ever called with the six existing manifests (BOT/SECRETS/MCP/CONFIG/OBS/CERTBOT); none contains `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`. With no `if changed \"<edge>\"` block, an edge-only delta reaches the end of the tick with no `err`/`marker` call. Confirmed at runtime, not statically: driving the REAL `autodeploy.sh` (git stub → only `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` changed, `main` advanced d…d → e…e) prints `main advanced …; computing component deltas` and `deploy complete` on stdout and emits **nothing** on stderr — no `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`. This is a `dynamic` hypothesis (the signal never fires) confirmed by observing the run, discriminating it from \"a delta was computed but a different signal fired\".\n\n**Defect origin (`caused_by`) — scope-of-work omission, story 8903.** The path-manifest + `changed`-detection deploy model was introduced by commits `479c3a57b4c0` and `463739cdb481`, both carrying `rebar-ticket: 8903-efb2-b73f-4e22` (Epic 88ab / story `gall-plume-adder`, autodeploy v1). ADR 0079 scoped v1 apply to the review-bot container and made Gerrit config detect-only, but the plan never enumerated the nginx edge in **either** the apply or the detect-only category. This is an omission / incomplete-implementation, not a regression: the edge was never detected, so there is no \"later change broke it\" commit — `git blame` on the manifest region names the CONFIG/OBS/CERTBOT authors, none of whom owned the edge. Attribution is **by scope-of-work** to 8903 (the story whose ACs the missing case falls under), not by introducing commit. Recorded via `--caused-by=8903-efb2-b73f-4e22`, close_class `plan_defect`. Date test: the omission predates any behavior transition (it never worked), consistent with an omission rather than a regression.\n\n**Test (RED→GREEN, held out, mutation-checked).** New `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_signals_nginx_edge.py` (mirrors `test_autodeploy_signals_gerrit_config.py`): drives the real `autodeploy.sh` where only `rebar.conf.template` changed and asserts `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` with `reason=nginx_edge_manual` and a `detail` naming `rebar.conf.template`. Verified legitimately RED first (asserted `None` — no marker — with the fix absent). The fix was written by a subagent that never saw the test; GREEN on restore. Mutation check (in a macOS `sandbox-exec` jail): re-seeding the root cause (`if changed \"$EDGE_PATHS\"` → `if false`) returns the test to RED, proving teeth. It asserts observable stderr output, not internal names, so it is not a change-detector.\n\n**Fix.** `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`: (1) new `EDGE_PATHS='infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template'` manifest with a comment explaining the DETECT-ONLY v1 boundary and the v2 deferral (epic 6d60); (2) a detect-only block mirroring `CONFIG_PATHS` exactly — `if changed \"$EDGE_PATHS\"; then err nginx_edge_manual \"…rebar.conf.template needs a MANUAL operator render + nginx reload…\"; log …; fi`. `observability.sh:232` already counts every `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR {` into the `deploy_errors` CloudWatch metric regardless of `reason`, so the miss becomes visible via the same always-on on-box journald path — no observability change, no CI-provider dependency (portable). No render / `nginx -t` / reload / rollback (deferred to epic 6d60).\n\n**Scope & safety.** Caller-dependency sweep: `EDGE_PATHS`/`nginx_edge_manual` are new symbols with no other callers; the block reuses existing `err`/`changed`/`marker` — only-incidental usage, clears the gate. Restoration not creation (restores parity with `CONFIG_PATHS`; legitimacy = incomplete-implementation, cited to 8903/ADR 0079 — completing approved work). No new dependency. No existing test weakened (new test only). Never touches the `gerrit` container; mutates no AWS box.\n\n**Siblings (Step 7).** Both axes converge on one confirmed sibling class: the host-nginx *includes* the edge template glob-includes are materialized by `compose-up.sh` (`materialize-opcert-guard.sh`, `materialize-mcp-upstream.sh`, the `mcp-upstream.conf` seed) and `compose-up.sh` itself — absent from every manifest and never re-run by the autodeploy loop (autodeploy re-runs only `install-observability.sh`/`install-certbot-timer.sh`/`fetch-secrets.sh`). Same silent-drift class, NOT covered by epic 6d60. Filed as **satiated-activated-aardwolf (5524-e353-2e2d-4dbe)**, linked `discovered_from` this bug. Not fixed here: it touches `nginx -s reload` apply semantics (the deferred v1→v2 boundary) and a distinct surface, outside the operator-approved Option A scope.\n\n**Residual risk.** (1) `mcp-upstream.conf` seed / materialize-script drift → ticketed (5524). (2) This change only makes the miss *visible*; a human still renders+reloads the edge (unattended auto-apply is epic 6d60, accepted per Option A). (3) The `deployed-sha`/`origin/main` divergence noted in the report is a separate cadence/backoff observation, not addressed here (accepted; out of this bug's mechanism).\n\n**Replication.** The report's scenario (main advances with only the edge changed) driven through the real `autodeploy.sh` entry point now emits the `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` signal instead of silently no-op'ing. Full scripts suite: 1307 passed, 3 skipped, no regressions.\n\n**Landing.** Change goes through Gerrit (`git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`); submittable only at `LLM-Review +1` AND `Verified +1`. The \"verified live at the edge\" / a61d-unblocked AC is a SEPARATE operator deploy after this lands (a shared-box mutation), not performed by this change. `caused_by`/close will be recorded on the close after the change is `Verified +1`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788112024255189644,"uuid":"1ec02239-ca91-4f6d-a29a-82ed0ae4cb9f"}